WEBVTT

00:00.860 --> 00:03.250
[MICHE] The odds of there being
any Titans

00:03.290 --> 00:05.800
in the hundred and forth
Cadet Corps are low.

00:07.257 --> 00:08.970
We've got multiple Titans
incoming from the south!

00:09.040 --> 00:12.440
Wall Rose has been compromised!

00:17.250 --> 00:19.680
[NARRATOR] Suspected by some
of unknowingly harboring

00:19.720 --> 00:21.520
the enemy among their ranks,

00:21.550 --> 00:24.990
the hundred and fourth Cadet
Corps was kept isolated.

00:25.020 --> 00:27.690
With the sudden emergence
of a Titan swarm,

00:27.720 --> 00:31.990
couriers were dispatched to
alert surrounding districts.

00:35.000 --> 00:36.330
[NANABA]
As you have guessed,

00:36.370 --> 00:39.670
today marks the darkest hour
in humanity's history!

00:39.700 --> 00:40.830
Don't lose heart.

00:40.870 --> 00:42.400
If ever we needed
to give our all,

00:42.440 --> 00:45.240
that time is now!
Look sharp!

00:45.270 --> 00:47.070
[NARRATOR]
However...

00:51.350 --> 00:52.510
[BOTH gasp]

00:52.550 --> 00:55.820
[MICHE] No! They're
coming at us full tilt!

00:55.890 --> 00:57.550
[HORSE 26A whinnies]

00:57.590 --> 00:59.450
[NARRATOR] Their origins
and how they got here

00:59.520 --> 01:01.120
remain a mystery.

01:01.190 --> 01:04.090
Mankind is still in the dark.

01:09.070 --> 01:11.230
[Yells]

01:11.270 --> 01:12.630
[MICHE screams]

01:12.700 --> 01:16.370
Ah, an exceptionally
clever idea, I must say.

01:17.740 --> 01:22.410
[Screams]

01:24.650 --> 01:29.620
♪ Opening Song  ♪

03:04.414 --> 03:05.847
 [MALE MESSENGER 27A]
Commander Pyxis!

03:05.888 --> 03:07.622
[Panting]

03:07.692 --> 03:09.266
Titans have been spotted, sir!

03:09.296 --> 03:12.875
We think Wall Rose
has been breached!

03:12.945 --> 03:14.620
[PYXIS growls lowly]

03:16.996 --> 03:19.903
[HORSE neighs]

03:19.933 --> 03:24.485
[EREN] Great. Somebody explain
to me what this means.

03:26.028 --> 03:29.998
[ARMIN] I don't know.
But they're Titans, right?

03:30.039 --> 03:32.675
Would they break a wall
with Titans in it?

03:32.715 --> 03:34.480
Wouldn't be the first time.

03:34.520 --> 03:37.096
It's how they
got into Shiganshina.

03:37.126 --> 03:39.232
[ARMIN]
That was a gate.

03:40.846 --> 03:43.152
Armin. What exactly
are you getting at?

03:43.182 --> 03:44.515
[MALE SOLDIER 27B]
Fall in!

03:44.555 --> 03:46.229
[ARMIN]
The walls are different.

03:46.259 --> 03:48.305
There are no signs
of stress, no cracks,

03:48.365 --> 03:50.340
no crevices between the rocks.

03:50.380 --> 03:53.718
We can't even really tell
how they were constructed.

03:55.623 --> 03:57.367
Suppose they're built
with the same stuff

03:57.398 --> 03:59.202
Annie's trapped herself in?

03:59.242 --> 04:01.247
[BOTH gasp]

04:01.277 --> 04:03.222
Must be versatile material,

04:03.252 --> 04:06.761
and we know it's virtually
indestructible.

04:07.934 --> 04:11.954
So the walls
are made of Titans?

04:11.984 --> 04:14.320
Section Commander!
Why are you taking so long?

04:14.360 --> 04:17.137
Please! They're leaving in five
minutes with or without us!

04:17.167 --> 04:18.541
You've got to wrap it up!

04:18.611 --> 04:21.819
Hold your horses,
I just need another moment.

04:22.491 --> 04:24.797
[Gasps]

04:24.827 --> 04:27.634
[LEVI]
Hange. Get moving.

04:27.674 --> 04:30.010
[HANGE] Uh, right!
Sorry! And our guest?

04:30.050 --> 04:32.586
He's been ready
to go for a while.

04:39.213 --> 04:41.218
[HORSE neighs]

04:41.258 --> 04:45.068
[MIKASA] Eren, you'll
get cold. Wear it tight.

04:45.098 --> 04:47.243
[HANGE]
Sorry to keep you waiting.

04:47.273 --> 04:49.880
Took longer to prepare
than I thought.

04:49.950 --> 04:51.454
[Gasps]

04:55.675 --> 04:59.986
He's, uh. He's a priest
from the Order of the Walls.

05:00.026 --> 05:03.164
I know! Ol' Nick and me
are thick as thieves!

05:03.234 --> 05:05.509
[Laughs]

05:05.540 --> 05:08.617
It's fine. Makes about
as much sense for him

05:08.647 --> 05:10.723
to be here as the rest
of us, don't'cha think?

05:10.793 --> 05:12.928
We're random.

05:12.998 --> 05:15.505
No, on the contrary.

05:15.545 --> 05:18.683
Erwin's thrown us
together for a reason.

05:18.723 --> 05:20.357
[MALE SOLDIER 27B]
Open the gate!

05:28.016 --> 05:29.119
[HORSE neighs]

05:29.189 --> 05:32.036
The status
of Wall Rose in unclear,

05:32.066 --> 05:34.372
but everything
up to Ehrmich is safe.

05:34.412 --> 05:36.578
That's the route
we'll be taking.

05:36.618 --> 05:37.981
Let's move out!

05:38.052 --> 05:40.297
[SOLDIERS]
Yes, sir!

05:40.327 --> 05:41.701
You heard 'im.

05:41.731 --> 05:43.606
[MOBLIT]
Sir!

05:57.621 --> 05:59.997
[ARMIN] This whole time,
Titans have been

06:00.037 --> 06:03.706
protecting us from other Titans.

06:14.453 --> 06:16.358
[EREN]
Wait, wait! Back up!

06:16.388 --> 06:17.521
You're joking, right?

06:17.561 --> 06:20.699
This guy knew?
He knew and he kept quiet?

06:20.739 --> 06:23.115
Uh-huh. Afraid so.

06:23.175 --> 06:26.594
Just about sums up
where we are with him.

06:26.624 --> 06:27.998
[Exhales]

06:28.068 --> 06:30.634
[HANGE] Cat's out of
the bag now, of course.

06:30.674 --> 06:32.850
He's not willing to talk yet,

06:32.910 --> 06:36.960
but we'll see how he feels
after a harsh dose of reality.

06:37.000 --> 06:38.634
Faith keeps him quiet.

06:38.665 --> 06:41.642
Firsthand experience, though?

06:41.682 --> 06:43.316
[EREN]
To hell with that!

06:43.356 --> 06:44.950
No! We're doing this backwards!

06:44.990 --> 06:46.494
If this son of bitch
knows something

06:46.524 --> 06:48.229
he needs to come out with it!

06:48.299 --> 06:50.073
Humanity's on
the brink of extinction

06:50.144 --> 06:52.850
and all you care about
is keeping your oath?

06:52.880 --> 06:55.427
[MIKASA]
Hey. Take it easy.

06:55.497 --> 06:58.003
You're still not
fully recovered.

06:58.775 --> 07:01.913
[LEVI] There's more than
one way to get at the truth.

07:01.953 --> 07:04.961
Granted I may not be
in top form at the moment,

07:05.031 --> 07:08.199
but it doesn't take much
strength to squeeze a trigger.

07:08.239 --> 07:10.876
That said. I'm genuinely
hoping I won't have to

07:10.916 --> 07:13.452
blow a hole in you
to settle this.

07:13.492 --> 07:14.926
How about you?

07:14.996 --> 07:16.901
[HANGE] Threatening him
doesn't work, Levi.

07:16.941 --> 07:18.976
Trust me on that.

07:19.006 --> 07:21.082
Agree with him or not,
there's no denying

07:21.122 --> 07:23.889
our priest here
is a man of principle.

07:23.929 --> 07:26.636
Which of course
leads me to wonder:

07:26.666 --> 07:30.285
if he's so unwilling to talk,
what in heaven's name

07:30.315 --> 07:34.295
do you imagine he's putting
above the fate of humanity?

07:36.500 --> 07:38.546
[SASHA] Up ahead, you see?
That's the village!

07:38.576 --> 07:40.019
[MALE SOLDIER 26G]
Where you're from?

07:40.049 --> 07:45.002
[SASHA] No, but it's close.
My people live the forest.

07:45.032 --> 07:47.107
It's okay. Go on.

07:47.177 --> 07:50.756
All right. Find your home
and raise the alarm.

07:50.787 --> 07:51.719
[SASHA]
Yes, sir!

07:51.759 --> 07:53.894
[HORSE neighs]

07:58.386 --> 08:01.123
[SASHA'S FATHER] Good lord!
Again with this?

08:01.163 --> 08:04.772
Sasha! You can't always
be stuffin' your face!

08:04.802 --> 08:06.677
Give it here!

08:06.747 --> 08:07.980
Spit it out!

08:08.020 --> 08:09.825
We're smoking that
for the winter!

08:09.855 --> 08:12.261
Oh, for cryin' out loud!

08:15.278 --> 08:17.384
[Yells]

08:21.534 --> 08:24.341
You little--
Show some restraint!

08:24.371 --> 08:26.878
[SASHA'S FATHER grunts]
Fine.

08:26.918 --> 08:28.752
Eat your fill.

08:28.823 --> 08:31.529
Hm! Idiot kid.

08:36.582 --> 08:39.229
[SASHA'S FATHER sighs]

08:40.562 --> 08:43.540
Sasha. Look around ya.

08:43.570 --> 08:46.888
Ever wonder how things
got to be the way they are?

08:46.918 --> 08:49.425
Why the forest is disappearing?

08:49.465 --> 08:52.643
Why game's so hard
to come by these days?

08:52.673 --> 08:56.081
Or doesn't it concern you?

08:56.121 --> 08:57.425
Sure it does.

08:57.455 --> 08:59.129
People are comin' in here
and helping themselves

08:59.159 --> 09:00.763
to what used to be ours.

09:00.803 --> 09:03.610
It's why I'm hungry
all the time.

09:03.640 --> 09:06.187
Yeah, that's true.

09:06.217 --> 09:07.891
On the face of it.

09:07.961 --> 09:09.535
But where else
you expect folks to go

09:09.565 --> 09:11.199
when they lose their homes?

09:11.240 --> 09:13.375
They've got a right
to live, don't they?

09:13.415 --> 09:15.380
It's their fault
for losing their homes.

09:15.420 --> 09:18.698
Not like that gives 'em
the right to steal.

09:18.728 --> 09:20.703
They lost their homes
'cause of Titans.

09:20.744 --> 09:23.581
Monsters punched a hole
clean through Wall Maria.

09:23.611 --> 09:27.130
Where else were
people gonna go?

09:27.190 --> 09:30.468
Wasn't their choice.
They had to survive somehow,

09:30.538 --> 09:34.418
so they cleared the forest
and used it for farmland.

09:36.924 --> 09:40.403
Maybe it's time
for us to let go.

09:40.443 --> 09:43.822
Surrender the old ways.

09:43.852 --> 09:45.426
We're not gonna starve.

09:45.456 --> 09:47.601
Government's willing
to pay us, y'know.

09:47.672 --> 09:49.536
We'll make money raising horses.

09:49.606 --> 09:52.283
[SASHA gasps] What? If we
turn our back on hunting,

09:52.313 --> 09:53.987
we turn our back on who we are!

09:54.028 --> 09:55.622
Why should I care about
what happens to the people

09:55.662 --> 09:56.965
who've always looked down as us

09:56.995 --> 09:58.569
like we were a bunch of savages?

09:58.639 --> 10:01.476
I'll tell you why.

10:01.516 --> 10:03.050
We're in this together.

10:03.090 --> 10:06.669
The world belongs to each
and every one of us.

10:06.700 --> 10:10.549
We're human.
Humans are social animals.

10:10.579 --> 10:12.254
It's all fine
and good to move to

10:12.284 --> 10:15.592
the beat of your own drum,
but when land is scarce,

10:15.632 --> 10:17.637
you've got to fall
in step with the herd.

10:17.707 --> 10:19.141
Think about the greater good.

10:19.211 --> 10:20.915
[SASHA]
No! I won't do it!

10:20.956 --> 10:22.249
We've lived here all our lives

10:22.289 --> 10:23.923
the way our ancestors
taught us to.

10:23.963 --> 10:25.597
I'm not gonna change!

10:25.637 --> 10:28.805
Screw the "greater good"!
What about us?

10:33.156 --> 10:34.329
Right, then.

10:34.430 --> 10:37.778
If that's how you really feel.

10:37.808 --> 10:39.111
[Inhales]

10:39.151 --> 10:41.487
Eke out a living
in these woods.

10:41.527 --> 10:45.838
Live by the old ways,
like the others.

10:45.868 --> 10:47.813
But I'll tell you something,

10:47.843 --> 10:50.791
you'd best be willing to
die by the old ways, too.

10:50.821 --> 10:52.525
[Gasps]

10:52.565 --> 10:54.701
[SASHA'S FATHER]
'Cause make no mistake, Sasha,

10:54.741 --> 10:57.207
trouble is coming
sooner or later.

10:57.247 --> 10:59.012
And when it does,

10:59.052 --> 11:00.555
there'll be
no begging for help

11:00.586 --> 11:04.305
from the people
you've turned your back on.

11:04.375 --> 11:05.869
If it means
the difference between

11:05.909 --> 11:08.546
being a part of something
larger than myself

11:08.616 --> 11:12.165
and scraping by on my own,
I say screw tradition.

11:12.235 --> 11:15.503
It's time to move on.

11:15.573 --> 11:17.147
What about you?

11:17.177 --> 11:20.125
Are you brave enough
to take that step with me?

11:20.155 --> 11:22.330
Trade the wilderness
of your ancestors

11:22.370 --> 11:25.007
for a share in civilization?

11:25.047 --> 11:28.917
Or is our fellow man
just not worth the hassle?

11:31.664 --> 11:34.341
[SASHA] How long
has it been? Three years?

11:34.381 --> 11:38.050
Surely he'd have had the sense
to pick up and leave by now.

11:41.439 --> 11:45.509
Impossible!
All the way out here?

11:48.897 --> 11:52.366
Can they really
have gotten this far?

11:52.406 --> 11:56.216
That's does it.
This place isn't safe anymore.

11:58.131 --> 12:00.236
[Gasps]

12:00.266 --> 12:04.276
[SASHA] Whoa.
When did that get built?

12:13.780 --> 12:21.209
[TITAN 27A chews]
[Squelching]

12:21.239 --> 12:34.523
[FEMALE VILLAGER 27A
breathes slowly]

12:41.510 --> 12:43.285
[Chirps]

12:45.390 --> 12:56.328
[FEMALE VILLAGER 27A
gasps and groans]

12:56.368 --> 13:06.493
[Music plays,
volume increases]

13:06.533 --> 13:09.240
[SASHA bellows]

13:15.366 --> 13:22.123
[SASHA grunts]

13:22.193 --> 13:24.759
[SASHA] Shit!
If I don't cut it off,

13:24.799 --> 13:26.564
it'll just keep healing!

13:26.634 --> 13:28.108
[Gasps]

13:28.148 --> 13:31.617
[Hollers]

13:31.657 --> 13:35.968
[FEMALE VILLAGER 27A groans]

13:36.008 --> 13:38.775
Oh no.

13:39.787 --> 13:45.973
[FEMALE VILLAGER 27A gasps]

13:46.003 --> 13:49.311
I'm so sorry. Forgive me.

13:53.201 --> 13:56.840
[Gasps]

14:03.036 --> 14:05.201
You got a name, sweetie?

14:07.918 --> 14:10.124
I know you're scared,
but it'll be okay.

14:10.194 --> 14:11.297
[GIRL 27A]
What will?

14:11.357 --> 14:15.036
Uh. Well, um,
actually, I, uh...

14:15.076 --> 14:17.813
Uh, easy now, easy.
Right, so.

14:17.883 --> 14:20.460
The thing is,
I'm going to take you--

14:20.490 --> 14:21.833
[Screams]

14:21.904 --> 14:23.838
You do this now? Really?

14:23.909 --> 14:25.974
Ugh! Wait for us!

14:26.014 --> 14:28.250
[Whistles]

14:28.290 --> 14:30.325
Okay. No need
to worry, understand?

14:30.425 --> 14:32.029
He'll be right back, I promise.

14:32.099 --> 14:34.545
How come you're talking
so nice to me?

14:34.606 --> 14:36.180
Huh?

14:41.032 --> 14:43.007
[Shrieks]

14:44.641 --> 14:46.044
[SASHA]
We need to run!

14:46.085 --> 14:48.922
[Panting]

14:48.992 --> 14:51.568
It's gonna be okay!

14:51.598 --> 14:55.619
No it won't.
Everyone's already gone.

14:55.689 --> 14:57.122
The whole village.

14:57.193 --> 14:59.859
Even though
Mama's legs were bad.

14:59.899 --> 15:02.636
They knew, and none
of them came to help her.

15:02.707 --> 15:05.484
All I could do was watch.

15:16.461 --> 15:18.496
--[Crash]
--[SASHA yells]

15:24.321 --> 15:26.687
Don't look back!
Just keep running!

15:29.334 --> 15:31.539
It's gonna be okay.

15:34.256 --> 15:36.191
[YMIR] You're startin'
to piss me off.

15:36.231 --> 15:37.695
Huh?

15:37.735 --> 15:40.873
[YMIR] Why you gotta be so
friggin' polite all the time?

15:40.913 --> 15:42.246
[Chuckles nervously]

15:42.286 --> 15:44.953
What, you above talking
like one of us plebes?

15:45.023 --> 15:48.933
Well, actually.
No, not at all.

15:48.973 --> 15:51.780
Oh yeah?
So why don't'cha, then?

15:51.810 --> 15:53.655
Scared we'll hear
where you're from

15:53.725 --> 15:55.660
if you let your guard down?

15:55.730 --> 15:57.134
That's it, isn't it?

15:57.164 --> 15:59.841
Oh, wow.
Kinda blows my mind.

15:59.911 --> 16:01.615
Why do you even care?

16:01.645 --> 16:04.021
I mean, it's like a wild boar
getting all bent outta shape

16:04.091 --> 16:06.628
'cause someone's bad-mouthing
him behind his back.

16:06.668 --> 16:08.643
Be honest: the military's
your last hope

16:08.673 --> 16:10.147
of being respectable.

16:10.177 --> 16:11.681
Your folks're probably
first cousins--

16:11.721 --> 16:13.224
Ymir, stop it!
You're being mean!

16:13.295 --> 16:14.959
Whatever! Hey,
you gonna pretend to be

16:14.999 --> 16:17.064
someone you're not for
the rest of your damn life,

16:17.134 --> 16:18.708
or you gonna be Sasha?

16:18.748 --> 16:20.683
Take it from me, honey:
acting like you think

16:20.713 --> 16:23.220
people want you to act
is a crock of shit.

16:23.260 --> 16:25.736
Don't censor yourself!

16:26.538 --> 16:30.047
Um. Thank you very much?

16:30.087 --> 16:31.721
I appreciate the advice.

16:31.751 --> 16:33.095
Really?

16:33.125 --> 16:36.373
[SASHA] Sorry, I-I'm not
really sure what to say.

16:36.403 --> 16:38.448
Leave her alone!
It's her life!

16:38.478 --> 16:42.960
If she wants to talk politely
to people, why doyoucare?

16:43.000 --> 16:45.636
Sasha is who she
chooses to be.

16:45.676 --> 16:48.483
It's called
reinventing yourself.

16:48.514 --> 16:51.321
Whatever she says,
it's still her.

16:51.361 --> 16:53.827
Heh. Well, aren't
we philosophical.

16:53.867 --> 16:56.173
I say however she tries
to sound on the outside,

16:56.213 --> 16:59.050
the inside Sasha'll always
be a pain in the ass.

16:59.120 --> 17:00.895
Knock it off!
Would it kill you

17:00.955 --> 17:03.331
to show some compassion
every now and again?

17:03.371 --> 17:06.539
[YMIR] E-Excuse me?
I'm just bein' real!

17:06.579 --> 17:08.584
--[YMIR] Compassion.
--[SASHA laughs]

17:08.654 --> 17:10.760
[YMIR] Hey!
What are you laughing at?

17:10.830 --> 17:13.497
[SASHA]
Uh. Nothing! Sorry!

17:20.524 --> 17:23.732
[SASHA] Really? Why is
that coming back now?

17:23.773 --> 17:26.580
Of all the stupid things
for me to dwell on.

17:26.620 --> 17:30.530
Still, it's the only thing
I can think about.

17:33.136 --> 17:35.482
[SASHA]
All right, listen.

17:35.512 --> 17:36.916
You're gonna be fine.

17:36.956 --> 17:38.820
Just keep following
the path we're on.

17:38.861 --> 17:41.337
Run as far away as you can.

17:41.367 --> 17:44.515
There'll be someone
willing to help. I promise.

17:44.545 --> 17:46.951
It may take you
a little while to find them.

17:46.991 --> 17:51.071
But keep on! You'll bump
into them eventually!

17:51.132 --> 17:53.878
Now go. Get out of here!

17:57.558 --> 18:00.395
Don't give up hope!

18:02.240 --> 18:04.415
[Panting]

18:15.754 --> 18:17.288
[SASHA]
If I can take out the eyes,

18:17.328 --> 18:19.864
it should buy us enough time.

18:24.957 --> 18:25.789
Eeh!

18:25.829 --> 18:29.037
Damn it. Only two left!

18:29.097 --> 18:31.513
Relax. It's nothing.

18:31.544 --> 18:35.123
Just a big...
slow-moving...

18:35.153 --> 18:36.797
...target!

18:38.832 --> 18:40.877
Bull's eye!

18:44.085 --> 18:48.206
Last arrow.
If I miss, that'll be it.

18:52.286 --> 18:57.629
End of story.
Period. I'll be...

18:57.700 --> 18:59.604
She'll be...

19:03.093 --> 19:09.539
[SASHA bellows]

19:14.662 --> 19:20.778
[TITAN 27A groans]

19:20.818 --> 19:22.622
[SASHA grunts]

19:26.703 --> 19:29.480
[SASHA] I slipped out
because of the blood.

19:29.520 --> 19:31.354
Now to find the girl!

19:31.385 --> 19:34.061
[Panting]

19:37.440 --> 19:38.442
[SASHA gasps]

19:38.513 --> 19:40.548
Is that Sasha?

19:58.313 --> 20:00.257
[SASHA'S FATHER] We've been
doing what we can.

20:00.288 --> 20:02.262
Giving horses
to folks who need 'em.

20:02.293 --> 20:04.037
That little girl
told us there was someone

20:04.107 --> 20:06.513
back behind her on the road.

20:06.543 --> 20:09.892
Said they helped.
Saved her, 'n fact.

20:09.962 --> 20:13.230
Apparently fought off
a Titan single-handed.

20:13.300 --> 20:15.676
[SASHA]
Mm.

20:15.706 --> 20:18.524
Nicely done.
I'm proud of ya.

20:18.554 --> 20:20.889
[Gasps]

20:20.930 --> 20:23.035
Thanks, Dad.

20:25.040 --> 20:27.516
It's good to be home.

20:30.063 --> 20:33.441
Conny, slow down!
Get ahold of yourself!

20:33.471 --> 20:36.419
There could be Titans
around every corner!

20:36.449 --> 20:38.624
Wait for us!

20:41.171 --> 20:43.476
This isn't real.

20:47.657 --> 20:52.209
Hello? Can anybody hear me?

20:52.269 --> 20:54.815
Somebody! Please!
It's Conny!

20:54.845 --> 20:58.194
I came home!

21:06.525 --> 21:08.429
Find my house!

21:11.377 --> 21:17.462
[CONNY] Dad. Mom.
Sunny and Martin!

21:17.532 --> 21:20.239
Please just be okay.

21:21.512 --> 21:22.315
[Gasps]

21:22.375 --> 21:24.520
[HORSE whinnies]

21:33.423 --> 21:35.758
[Breathes quaveringly]

21:35.789 --> 21:38.034
What are you doing?
Get back!

21:38.104 --> 21:41.844
But it, it's my house.

21:41.884 --> 21:43.147
I...

21:43.187 --> 21:45.022
Conny.

21:45.062 --> 21:46.796
Cadets, fall back!

21:46.836 --> 21:49.273
[FEMALE SOLDIER 26B]
I'll scout out the area!

21:51.047 --> 21:53.984
What the hell?
This is new.

21:54.025 --> 21:55.899
Can it move?

21:55.929 --> 21:58.706
[FEMALE SOLDIER 26B]
Not with those legs.

21:58.736 --> 22:00.982
[GELGAR]
But... then...

22:01.052 --> 22:03.017
I don't understand.

22:03.057 --> 22:05.935
How did it even get here?

22:10.646 --> 22:15.669
♪ Closing Song ♪
